  "description": "A durable, queryable log store for ASP.NET Core apps built with Rask — kept in a SQLite file of its own, or in the application's PostgreSQL or SQL Server database through EF Core, with no agent and no hosted log service. Registers a standard `ILoggerProvider`, so it captures exactly what every other sink sees, buffers entries through a bounded channel that never blocks the caller, and writes them in batches on a background service. Retention is enforced by age and by row count, swept in short pages so locks are never held for long. Pairs with Rask.Dashboard, whose Logs page reads the store. Server-side.",
